        &lt;kb_instructions&gt;&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt; To create a new article:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol id="t_CreateAKnowledgeArticle__steps_ez1_lwl_ls" style="list-style-position: inside;"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Navigate to &lt;strong&gt;Self-Service &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;gt; &lt;strong&gt;Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;Create an Article.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Fill in the fields in the displayed form.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;Submit&lt;/strong&gt; to publish the article. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Note: &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul style="list-style-position: inside;"&gt;&lt;li&gt;If the knowledge base in which you want to publish the article is assigned with an approval workflow, the article will be added to an approval queue. Once it is approved, the article will be available for the end users. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If the knowledge base in which you want to publish the article was not assigned with an approval workflow, the article will be available for the end users immediately.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;]]&gt;&lt;/kb_instructions&gt;
        &lt;kb_introduction&gt;&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;As a default, users with at least one role can create and edit knowledge articles. These users are known as knowledge contributors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style="list-style-position: inside;"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Users without any role can read articles and submit feedback, however they cannot create or edit articles.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;To create an article, you must have &amp;#34;Can contribute&amp;#34; user criteria for the knowledge base in which you want to create an article.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Each knowledge base can have customized user criteria that will effect the default settings of access to articles. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;]]&gt;&lt;/kb_introduction&gt;
